  "observations": {
    "nyuv2_0001": [
      "Room/cabinet/chair scene: L and J visibly reduce broad wall and cabinet interior relative error in metric depth compared with B0; R improves less at best and more at final. Their broad object layout remains recognizable.",
      "Boundary overlay remains mostly missed-GT red at the right cabinet/counter and chair boundary. L has zero matched boundary F1 at best and final; J falls from approximately 0.018 to zero. Low AbsRel here does not establish sharp boundaries.",
      "R retains a small number of matched cyan pixels and has slightly higher F1 than B0, despite L/J giving lower overall AbsRel. A zero thresholded-boundary F1 does not mean the predicted depth image is spatially constant."
    ],
    "nyuv2_0770": [
      "Kitchen/stove scene is a clear overall-error counterexample: B0 has darker, smaller error regions; all three adapted routes have higher AbsRel, with R showing particularly broad cabinet/stove error that increases from best to final.",
      "L and J recover more cyan matched boundary segments along the bottom of the upper cabinets and the left counter than B0/R. Yet hood, dish, and several cabinet edges remain missed.",
      "Thus better thresholded boundary F1 coexists with worse overall depth accuracy in this fixed sample. It is not valid to claim either all structures improved or all images improved."
    ],
    "nyuv2_1449": [
      "Dining room: the three adapted methods reduce broad foreground chair/table error relative to B0 at the best checkpoint. Error along chair outlines, table reflections and the hanging fixture remains.",
      "All routes recover much of the large chair-back outlines, but several thin chair legs and seat boundaries remain red. R largely retains the B0 outline pattern; L/J do not visibly resolve the missing thin structures.",
